    "text": "Let the shortest distance between the lines $\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y-\\alpha}{-1}=\\frac{z-3}{1}$ and $\\frac{x+3}{-3}=\\frac{y+7}{2}=\\frac{z-\\beta}{4}$ be $3 \\sqrt{30}$. Then the positive value of $5 \\alpha+\\beta$ is"
